<% @title = "Amber 2 — Web development, crystal clear" %>
<% @meta = "Amber 2.0 beta brings a modern, typed web framework and a new cross-platform Amber CLI to Crystal developers." %>

<div class="release-strip">
  <div class="site-container">
    <span class="release-pill">New</span>
    <span>Amber 2.0.0-beta.2 and Amber CLI 2.0.2 are ready to evaluate.</span>
    <a href="/blog/2026/07/31/amber-2-beta-2">Read the release notes →</a>
  </div>
</div>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="site-container hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Crystal web framework</p>
      <h1>Web development, <em>crystal clear.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Amber 2 gives Crystal developers a focused framework for typed, high-performance web applications—now paired with a new cross-platform CLI and an ECR-first web template.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/v2/getting-started/installation">Start with Amber V2</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/amberframework/amber" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <p class="support-note">Beta support: Apple Silicon macOS and x86_64 Linux · Crystal 1.20+</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="/assets/brand/amber-grant-gemma-hero.webp" width="1800" height="1196" alt="">
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="site-container terminal-wrap" aria-label="Create an Amber V2 application">
  <div class="terminal">
    <div class="terminal-toolbar">
      <span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span>
      <span class="terminal-title">amber-v2 — zsh</span>
    </div>
    <pre><code><span class="terminal-prompt">$</span> <span class="terminal-command">brew install amberframework/amber_cli/amber_cli</span>
<span class="terminal-success">✓ Amber CLI 2.0.2 installed</span>
<span class="terminal-prompt">$</span> <span class="terminal-command">amber new my_app --type web</span>
<span class="terminal-accent">Created my_app with Amber 2.0.0-beta.2</span>
<span class="terminal-prompt">$</span> <span class="terminal-command">cd my_app &amp;&amp; shards install &amp;&amp; amber watch</span>
<span class="terminal-muted">Listening at http://localhost:3000</span></code></pre>
  </div>
</div>

<main>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Framework core</p>
          <h2>A smaller surface.<br>A clearer path.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Amber 2 concentrates on the web framework itself: routing, controllers, rendering, configuration, and the primitives needed to ship a Crystal service with confidence.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">A</span>
          <h3>Typed configuration</h3>
          <p>Catch configuration mistakes at startup and keep environment behavior explicit.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">{ }</span>
          <h3>Compiled routing</h3>
          <p>Describe HTTP routes with a focused DSL backed by Crystal’s compiler.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">&lt;%</span>
          <h3>ECR-first views</h3>
          <p>Ship server-rendered HTML with Crystal’s native embedded templates.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">↗</span>
          <h3>Schema API</h3>
          <p>Define request and response contracts close to the application code that uses them.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">⚡</span>
          <h3>Crystal performance</h3>
          <p>Compile to a native binary and take advantage of Crystal 1.21’s multithreaded runtime.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">CLI</span>
          <h3>Cross-platform CLI</h3>
          <p>Install a purpose-built binary, generate a web app, and stay in one development loop.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tinted">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The ecosystem</p>
          <h2>Three tools.<br>One visual language.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Amber is the supported V2 beta core. Grant and Gemma are preview ecosystem projects, documented honestly so evaluators know where the release boundary is.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ecosystem-grid">
        <article class="ecosystem-card amber">
          <div class="ecosystem-mark">A</div>
          <h3>Amber</h3>
          <p>The web framework: controllers, routing, rendering, configuration, channels, jobs, mailers, and application structure.</p>
          <span class="status-badge">V2 beta supported</span>
          <a href="/docs/v2">Explore Amber docs →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="ecosystem-card teal">
          <div class="ecosystem-mark">G</div>
          <h3>Grant</h3>
          <p>An ActiveRecord-style ORM for Crystal, evolving independently from the Amber 2 framework release.</p>
          <span class="status-badge">Ecosystem preview</span>
          <a href="/docs/v2/guides/models/grant">Review preview guide →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="ecosystem-card violet">
          <div class="ecosystem-mark">Gm</div>
          <h3>Gemma</h3>
          <p>A focused file-attachment toolkit for Crystal applications, with storage and validation building blocks.</p>
          <span class="status-badge">Ecosystem preview</span>
          <a href="/docs/v2/guides/uploads">Review preview guide →</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Choose your path</p>
          <h2>From curious<br>to running.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The V2 guide is organized around the decisions a new evaluator actually has to make—platform, installation, project creation, and beta boundaries.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="journey-grid">
        <article class="journey-card">
          <span class="journey-number">01 / INSTALL</span>
          <h3>Set up macOS or Linux</h3>
          <p>Follow one verified path for Apple Silicon macOS or x86_64 Linux and confirm both Crystal and Amber CLI versions.</p>
          <a href="/docs/v2/getting-started/installation">Open installation guide →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="journey-card">
          <span class="journey-number">02 / CREATE</span>
          <h3>Generate the web template</h3>
          <p>See exactly what <code>amber new --type web</code> creates, which versions it pins, and how to start it.</p>
          <a href="/docs/v2/guides/web-template">Open web template guide →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="journey-card">
          <span class="journey-number">03 / EVALUATE</span>
          <h3>Understand the beta</h3>
          <p>Know the supported release core, preview ecosystem boundaries, and what to include in a useful issue report.</p>
          <a href="/docs/v2/beta-support">Open beta support guide →</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <div>
          <h2>Build something clear.</h2>
          <p>Install Amber CLI 2.0.2, generate the ECR web template, and help shape Amber 2 before the stable release.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button" href="/docs/v2/getting-started/installation">Start the V2 guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
